      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T17:09:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you\u0027re right; the non-executing lanes could have gotten different values back from the `push_slots` call, versus the values that they currently hold. I don\u0027t think there\u0027s any case where this could change the program\u0027s correctness. The values in the dead lanes can be different, but those dead lanes should never get stored back to the slots, and we shouldn\u0027t be making any decisions that matter based on the contents of a dead lane. We do make decisions based on \"which lanes are active\" (the execution mask), but not \"the values stored in dead-lane slots.\"\n\nI guess if we implemented `dFdx` as a lane shuffle, and had code with a uniformity violation, we could observe a difference, but that\u0027s OK, I think.",
      "parentUuid": "8552cc5e_079c1865",
